WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:04.650
If we are serious about preventing climate
change, we need to be pumping a lot less of

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:09.130
this into the atmosphere.

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:13.580
That is the message in a new UN report.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:17.110
Its authors warn of a growing "Emissions Gap"
between rising emissions and the reductions

00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:21.140
needed to achieve the goals set out in the
Paris Climate accords.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:26.510
Worldwide emissions have to be cut by a quarter
by 2030 to keep global warming at 2 degrees

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:35.070
Celsius above pre-industrial levels, and avoid
drastic consequences, says the report.

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:41.170
And the biggest elephant in the room that
we refuse to see is the risk that it poses

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:47.239
to everything we like and appreciate in this
planet.

00:00:47.239 --> 00:00:58.690
Whether bio-diversity is your thing or sustainable
finance or the health of the planet, or people

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:05.369
or prosperity or peace, human movements...
you just pick up anything you like, everything

00:01:05.369 --> 00:01:06.590
is at risk.

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:12.149
At a UN summit in the Polish mining town of
Katowice starting Sunday, delegates will hammer

00:01:12.149 --> 00:01:21.639
out a plan to meet the Paris accords, a task
which seems much harder than

00:01:21.639 --> 00:02:58.739
they

00:02:58.739 --> 00:03:55.250
first imagined.

